Failure criteria: 
- FC1 (order): |p_measured − p_declared| > 0.25 → FAIL.
- FC2 (monotonicity): errors must decrease monotonically by ≥ 1.8× per refinement (for p=2) — i.e., e_h/e_{h/2} ≥ 1.8; else FAIL.
- FC3 (residual): the discrete residual of the exact solution under the discretization must converge at order ≥ p_declared − tol (truncation-error test): plug MS1 into the scheme; residual → 0 at order 2. This is the "exact-solution residual" acceptance item.
- FC4 (invariant): energy drift in the homogeneous Dirichlet pulse test ≤ 1e-10 relative.
- FC5 (detection/negative control): the defective scheme must yield p_measured ≈ 1 and be flagged FAIL by FC1. This is the anti-falsifier requirement — protocol must detect a wrong order.
- FC6 (stability): no NaN/Inf; CFL λ ≤ 0.9 (for the standard scheme; shifted stencil also λ ≤ 1 but margin).
- G-NUM verdict aggregation: PASS iff FC1–FC4 pass on scheme A AND FC5 detects scheme B. Cross-implementation: worker 12 vs worker 13 measured orders must agree within 0.15 (per stop rule "agree within tolerance").

