Backward Euler + Thomas implementation:
Op = D2 with Dirichlet: for interior points j=1..n-1: (v[j-1]-2v[j]+v[j+1])/h², with v[0]=v[n]=0.
Backward Euler system: v_{k+1} = v_k + dt w_{k+1}; w_{k+1} = w_k + dt A v_{k+1}, where A = op matrix.
=> w_{k+1} - dt A v_{k+1} = w_k
   v_{k+1} - dt w_{k+1} = v_k
From second: v_{k+1} = v_k + dt w_{k+1}. Substitute into first:
w_{k+1} - dt A (v_k + dt w_{k+1}) = w_k
=> (I - dt² A) w_{k+1} = w_k + dt A v_k
=> solve tridiagonal M w_{k+1} = rhs, M = I - dt²A.
A has diag -2/h², off +1/h². M diag = 1 + 2dt²/h², off = -dt²/h². Then v_{k+1} = v_k + dt w_{k+1}.
Boundary: w[0]=w[n]=0? For Dirichlet v=0 at walls for all t; w = v_t = 0 at walls. So solve only interior (size n-1), with boundary contributions zero. Thomas on interior system.

Thomas algorithm for tridiagonal with constant coefficients (a=offdiag, b=diag, c=offdiag):
```
def thomas(a, b, c, d):
    n = len(d); cp = np.empty(n); dp = np.empty(n)
    cp[0] = c[0]/b[0]; dp[0] = d[0]/b[0]
    for i in range(1,n):
        m = b[i] - a[i]*cp[i-1]
        cp[i] = c[i]/m
        dp[i] = (d[i] - a[i]*dp[i-1])/m
    x = np.empty(n); x[-1] = dp[-1]
    for i in range(n-2,-1,-1):
        x[i] = dp[i] - cp[i]*x[i+1]
    return x
```
With constant a,b,c: b = 1+2r, a=c=-r, r = dt²/h².
At the walls, d gets no boundary contributions (v=0, w=0 there) ✓.

Global order: backward Euler temporal error O(dt) = O(h) → dominant → measured order 1 ✓.

